**Exploring smoothing options**

I'm thinking about whether a simple extra smoothing will do the trick. Maybe I could use a short moving average of recent current ratios across the last kernel and block frames, which might better approximate the kernel average. In the deterministic state, since block frames are 256 and kernel frames are 2048, I wonder if the wrapper could derive the block frames. I could also consider adding a `ratio_history` vector of recent chunk ratios, averaging the last 8 to better manage outcomes without complicating the smoothing constant.
