I took a look at removing the helper function, and now I'm considering reintroducing it. It might be simpler to use a weighted average across recent ratios, maybe even a triangular method to de-emphasize older data. The p99 outlier suggests there could be a boundary issue with exact ratio resets. However, the p95 improvement shows progress, and we need to get below 3.29. Combining modest smoothing with window averaging is worth exploring — I think it could yield better results!
