**Summarizing changes and checks**

I need to mention the changes made in [src/stream/processor.rs] at lines 24-25 (const), 399-450 (state fields and helper), and 1571 (average/slew application). The deterministic dual-plane adapter now maintains a rolling per-chunk ratio window aligned with one RT kernel, sending a lightly slewed average ratio to the RT backend instead of just the latest callback ratio.  

For checks, `cargo test --release --test quality_gates quality_gate_dual_plane_fast_modulation_artifacts` failed but showed improvement, while the other quality gate passed. 

The remaining risk is that Stage 1 exit criteria are still unmet due to ongoing issues with the fast-modulation gate.
